ISO-10303-21;
HEADER;
FILE_DESCRIPTION(('ViewDefinition[DesignTransferView]'),'2;1');
FILE_NAME('bonsai-door-flipped.ifc','2026-11-25T00:00:00',('IfcSheet'),('IfcSheet'),'hand-written in the shape IfcOpenShell 0.8 / Bonsai writes','gen_fixture.py','');
FILE_SCHEMA(('IFC4'));
ENDSEC;
DATA;
/* #831: bonsai-door-symbols.ifc (see its own note below) with one more door, D03, the entrance door's type (DOOR-900-PLAN,
   SINGLE_SWING_LEFT) flipped as Bonsai's "Flip" leaves it: rotated 180 degrees about Z, its origin moved to the other end of the
   opening on the wall's other (interior) face. D03 stands in its own opening in the south wall at x 4.0 to 4.9; its placement's origin
   is at (4.9, 0.3), local X along IFC -X, local Y along IFC -Y. */
/* #831: one storey of 2.7 m walls, Bonsai-style. Exterior walls 0.3 m (footprint (0,0) (6,0) (9,3) (9,7) (0,7), the second wall oblique
   at 45 degrees), layers to the inside, material layer set usage and Pset_WallCommon.IsExternal; a 0.1 m partition at x = 5.
   Each door and window fills a real IfcOpeningElement (IfcRelVoidsElement, IfcRelFillsElement), is placed relative to it, and maps its
   body from its type (IfcRepresentationMap), as Bonsai writes them. As IfcOpenShell's feature.add_filling leaves them, no
   IfcRelContainedInSpatialStructure contains the doors and windows: they are on the storey only through the wall they fill.
   Each type also maps a Plan / Body / PLAN_VIEW Curve2D symbol, as Bonsai writes one.
   D01: 0.9 m entrance door in the south wall at x 2.0 to 2.9, SINGLE_SWING_LEFT; its symbol's swing is a trimmed IfcEllipse.
   D02: 0.8 m door in the partition at y 3.3 to 4.1, SINGLE_SWING_RIGHT; its leaf and swing are one IfcCompositeCurve (a polyline and a
   trimmed IfcCircle). W01: 1.2 m window (DOUBLE_PANEL_VERTICAL) in the oblique wall, 1.5 to 2.7 m along it, sill 0.9 m; its symbol is
   IfcPolylines. W02: 0.9 m window (SINGLE_PANEL) in the north wall, 3.0 to 3.9 m along it from (9,7); its symbol is deliberately 5 m
   off the window (a broken one, which the plan does not draw). */
